      "math_academy_id": "q-20061",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Scalar Triple Products Using Its Properties",
      "problem": "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $3a\\cdot (6b\\times c)=90.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a\\cdot (6b\\times c) & =90 \\\\ 3\\cdot 6\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =90 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
